IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), piece er4: the types that more than one er4 module uses.
-- Nouns only: no rules. Every type and constructor begins `er4 ` so that, after the merge, none can clash
-- with another piece's (the keel's convention). Quotations are copied from SOR-96-332.txt by script.

§ `Kinds of wage-loss plan (Part III)`

-- The definition of "plan" in reg 60 names four kinds of plan, whose standards are regs 63, 64, 65 and 66.
-- src:1012 | 60 The definition in this section applies to this Part.
-- src:1013 | plan means a wage-loss plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer, and includes a Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan and an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan referred to in sections 63, 64, 65 and 66, respectively. (régime)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 60 (src:1012-1013)
DECLARE `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan` IS ONE OF
    `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan`                              -- reg 63
    `er4 a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`                      -- reg 64
    `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`                    -- reg 65
    `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`          -- reg 66
    `er4 another wage-loss plan`                               -- a plan of none of the four named kinds

§ `Two persons caring for the same child under different regimes (Parts III.1 and III.2)`

-- Regs 76.21(2) and 76.42(2) turn on which of the two applicants "made the earlier application": the person claiming
-- under the Act (a claimant under section 23, or a self-employed person under section 152.05) or the provincial applicant.
-- src:1257 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), where one of the two persons referred to in subsection (1) has applied for and is entitled to receive benefits under section 23 of the Act (referred to in this section as “the claimant”) and the other person has applied for and is entitled to receive provincial benefits (referred to in this section as “the provincial applicant”), unless they have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks of such benefits they will each respectively apply for or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks of benefits,
-- src:1258 | (a) if the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act is an even number, the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant is half that number; and
-- src:1259 | (b) if that number is an odd number,
-- src:1260 | (i) where the claimant made the earlier application, one week of those benefits plus half of the remaining weeks of benefits is payable to the claimant, and
-- src:1261 | (ii) where the provincial applicant made the earlier application, half the number of weeks of benefits remaining, after deducting one week, are payable to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(2) (src:1257-1261)
DECLARE `er4 Who made the earlier application` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application`
    `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application`
